    "body": "claimed: sn3ro (Claude Code, Opus 5.5) · 2026-11-26 23:34 UTC · worktree/branch sn3ro:issue/4081-laser-kinds · plan: three slices, each a draft PR with `Refs #4081`, on the waterjet pattern (#1881, #1883).\n\n1. A `laser` machine kind (an XY gantry, an optional Z, no spindle, no rotary) and a laser head tool kind with stated cut rows (thickness, kerf, power percent, pierce time). No cutting value is inferred.\n2. A Laser Profile operation on the shared `motion::sheet` kernel: kerf offset, per-chain side and direction, leads and pierce from the plasma model, refusal by name when the kerf does not fit. It uses the DXF sketch chains as the plasma profile does.\n3. A laser post dialect: Grbl 1.1 laser mode (`M4` dynamic power, `S` as power), from the public Grbl wiki. The MCP surface goes through `add_operation` / `edit_operation`, as for the waterjet. Docs follow.\n\nThe last slice says `Fixes #4081`.\n",
